// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHICH BUILD IS ACTUALLY RUNNING.
//
// This exists because of a real half-hour that should not have happened. Files
// were written to the right folder, six checks passed on disk, and the app on
// screen still had the old voice and the old face. Neither of us could tell
// whether that was a stale browser cache, a stale folder, or a different
// computer entirely — because nothing on screen said what it was.
//
// "Looks the same to me" is not a bug report anyone can act on. It becomes one
// the moment the screen can answer "same as WHAT?".
//
// So the version is printed where it can be read: small in the nav bar, and in
// full at the top of the Grown-Up Corner. Every future update bumps VERSION and
// adds a line to CHANGES. If the number on screen is not the number in the
// message, the update did not land — and that is now a five-second check
// instead of a guessing game.
//
// Her brother's app has the same thing (config/buildStamp.js) for the same
// reason. It was added there after the same confusion.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

